  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1233 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nLate this week and into the weekend, the high pressure builds in \nover the Four Corners Region. As a result, monsoon moisture will be \ngreatly diminished in our region, leading to a return to drier and \nhotter conditions through the weekend. Some isolated POPs do remain \nover the mountains, likely from elevated heating and the lingering \nmid-level moisture, but little if any wetting rains are expected. \nHigh temperatures will continue to increase, with the plains rising \nback into the triple digits while the interior valleys see high-80s \nto low-90s. More spotty critical fire weather conditions will be \npossible, over the central mountains on Thursday, and potentially \nover gap flow areas and the San Luis Valley on Friday.",
